  id: Deep_cervicoauricular_muscle.L
  partName: Deep_cervicoauricular_muscle.L
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'This muscle connects the neck region to the ear and is responsible for moving
    the ear backward. It plays a role in directional hearing by allowing the ear
    to adjust its position in response to sounds. '
  - Although small, it contributes to sensory awareness and environmental responsiveness.
    It works alongside other auricular muscles to provide precise control over ear
    movements, enhancing the ability to detect and localize sounds.
